## snake
animal-snake = snake
animal-snake-more = More about the snake
mission-snake-facts-kiga = scales
mission-snake-facts-klasse1 = I have no legs. I wiggle along. I like warmth.
mission-snake-facts-klasse2 = Snakes have no legs and glide on their belly. Their skin is dry and smooth, not slimy. When they have grown, they slip out of their old skin. Our snake is very friendly.
mission-snake-facts-klasse3 = Snakes have no legs and move along using strong muscles all over their body. They are cold-blooded: only when they have warmed up in a warm spot do they wake up. They "smell" with their tongue. When they have grown, they slip out of their old skin like a jumper that is too tight. Our corn snake is completely harmless.

# loc_stone_wall
mission-snake-riddle-loc_stone_wall-kiga = wall
mission-snake-riddle-loc_stone_wall-klasse1 = I am long and smooth. It is warm here. I lie between rocks.
mission-snake-riddle-loc_stone_wall-klasse2 = The snake lies at the foot of a long, low row of stacked rocks. The rocks are still warm from the day, and soft moss grows between them.
mission-snake-riddle-loc_stone_wall-klasse3 = Snakes love warmth, and they get it from the sun. Our snake lies where flat grey rocks are stacked in a long, low row. Even now at night they are still a little warm, and soft green moss grows in the gaps. The row ends right at the back, in the corner by the hedge.

# loc_pumpkins
mission-snake-riddle-loc_pumpkins-kiga = pumpkins
mission-snake-riddle-loc_pumpkins-klasse1 = Here lie fat round things. They are orange. The vines are rough.
mission-snake-riddle-loc_pumpkins-klasse2 = The snake has hidden between big, round, orange fruits lying on the ground. Huge, rough leaves spread above them.
mission-snake-riddle-loc_pumpkins-klasse3 = Something long has curled up in one corner of the garden. All around the snake lie fat, smooth fruits in bright orange, some as big as a child's head. Long vines with huge, rough leaves creep over the ground. It is hard to see where the fruits end and the snake begins.

# loc_rowing_boat
mission-snake-riddle-loc_rowing_boat-kiga = boat
mission-snake-riddle-loc_rowing_boat-klasse1 = I lie under wood. It is blue. Two oars lean on it.
mission-snake-riddle-loc_rowing_boat-klasse2 = The snake has slipped under something big made of wood. It is painted blue and lies upside down in the grass. Two long oars lean beside it.
mission-snake-riddle-loc_rowing_boat-klasse3 = Once two children rowed in it; now it lies upside down in the grass and works as a roof. The blue paint is already peeling, and two long oars lean beside its round belly. It is dry and warm underneath, just right for a snake.

mission-snake-home = Great! The snakes are home again.

## chameleon
animal-chameleon = chameleon
animal-chameleon-more = More about the chameleon
mission-chameleon-facts-kiga = colours
mission-chameleon-facts-klasse1 = I change my colour. My eyes turn around. My tail curls up.
mission-chameleon-facts-klasse2 = Chameleons can change their colour when they are happy or cross or when it gets cooler. Their eyes turn independently, so they look in two directions at once. They hold on tight with their long tail.
mission-chameleon-facts-klasse3 = Chameleons change colour not only to hide, but also when they are happy, cross, or when it gets warmer or colder. Each eye turns on its own, so the animal looks forward and backward at the same time. With its long, sticky tongue it snaps crickets out of the air, faster than you can blink. Its tail can curl up and holds the animal tight.

# loc_lanterns
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_lanterns-kiga = lanterns
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_lanterns-klasse1 = I sit up high. Colourful lights glow around me. Red, yellow and blue.
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_lanterns-klasse2 = The chameleon sits on a branch in a tree full of paper lamps. They glow red, yellow, green and blue and sway gently.
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_lanterns-klasse3 = No fruit grows in this tree, only lights: many round paper lamps hang on thin strings among the leaves. They glow red, yellow, green and blue and sway gently to and fro. The chameleon sits on a branch right in the middle of them, and because it can change its colour, it is hard to spot.

# loc_palm
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_palm-kiga = palm
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_palm-klasse1 = My tree has no branches. Big fans grow on top. Brown nuts hang from them.
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_palm-klasse2 = The chameleon clings to a slim tree without branches. The trunk is rough, and right at the top grow huge leaves like big fans. Brown nuts hang below them.
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_palm-klasse3 = This tree looks different from all the others in the garden: its trunk is slim and rough and has not a single twig. Right at the top, big feathery leaves spread out like a giant fan. Thick brown coconuts hang between them. The chameleon holds on with its tail to one of the lowest leaf stalks.

# loc_vine_arch
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_vine_arch-kiga = arch
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_vine_arch-klasse1 = Green curtains hang here. Pink flowers bloom. A beam lies on top.
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_vine_arch-klasse2 = The chameleon sits on the beam of a wooden gateway. Green creepers with pink flowers grow on it and hang down like curtains.
mission-chameleon-riddle-loc_vine_arch-klasse3 = Anyone who wants to walk through this wooden gateway must first push aside curtains of green creepers. Delicate pink flowers grow on them and a thick beam lies across the top. The chameleon sits there, very still and almost as green as the creepers.

mission-chameleon-home = Great! The chameleons are home again.

## poison_dart_frog
animal-poison_dart_frog = poison dart frog
animal-poison_dart_frog-more = More about the poison dart frog
mission-poison_dart_frog-facts-kiga = colourful
mission-poison_dart_frog-facts-klasse1 = I am very colourful. I am very small. I like to hop.
mission-poison_dart_frog-facts-klasse2 = Poison dart frogs are tiny but very colourful. Their bright colours say: Leave me alone! They live in the warm, wet rainforest. Here in the zoo they are harmless and eat little flies.
mission-poison_dart_frog-facts-klasse3 = Poison dart frogs live in the rainforest of South America. Their strong colours are a warning: in the wild some are poisonous, so enemies leave them alone. The poison comes from their food in the rainforest, so here in the zoo the frogs are harmless. Tadpoles hatch from the eggs, and the father carries them on his back to the water.

# loc_stepping_stones
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_stepping_stones-kiga = stepping stones
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_stepping_stones-klasse1 = The ground is soft. Everything is wet. It squelches softly.
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_stepping_stones-klasse2 = The frog sits on a row of round, smooth plates leading across wet green moss. Anyone who steps near hears a soft squelch.
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_stepping_stones-klasse3 = The ground here is always wet and soft as a sponge. Anyone who wants dry feet hops across a row of round, smooth plates that lie like little islands in the green moss. On one of them sits the little frog, very still, with shiny skin.

# loc_ferns
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_ferns-kiga = ferns
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_ferns-klasse1 = It is damp here. Giant fronds grow. Everything is green.
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_ferns-klasse2 = The frog sits under giant green fronds that bend over it like umbrellas. It is damp, and a fine mist hangs above the ground.
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_ferns-klasse3 = Next to an old tree stump grows a whole forest of giant, feathery fronds. They are as tall as a child and bend over like green umbrellas. It is cool and damp, and a fine mist hangs over the ground. Something colourful glows in between.

# loc_rain_barrel
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_rain_barrel-kiga = rain barrel
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_rain_barrel-klasse1 = It drips: tip, tip, tip. A tub stands by me. It is made of wood.
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_rain_barrel-klasse2 = The frog sits next to a big wooden tub. Water drips into it from a little roof: tip, tip, tip.
mission-poison_dart_frog-riddle-loc_rain_barrel-klasse3 = Under a small eave stands a big round wooden tub with dark iron rings. Water drips in steadily from the pipe: tip, tip, tip. A big leaf leans against the rim, and right underneath it sits the frog, listening.

mission-poison_dart_frog-home = Great! The poison dart frogs are home again.

